1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,562
You'd never expect a visitor from another star.

2
00:00:02,582 --> 00:00:05,638
But in 2017, one raced past the Sun

3
00:00:05,658 --> 00:00:07,453
and sped up. What was it, actually?

4
00:00:07,473 --> 00:00:10,373
Comets speed up by releasing gas. But ʻOumuamua

5
00:00:10,393 --> 00:00:13,093
had no visible cloud and no tail.

6
00:00:13,113 --> 00:00:17,622
In 2023, scientists suggested trapped hydrogen, made by cosmic

7
00:00:17,642 --> 00:00:20,425
rays in its ice, gave it a gentle push.

8
00:00:20,445 --> 00:00:23,060
Best guess. It's long gone, so we can't check.

9
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:25,875
Five more solar system mysteries are on the channel.
